Sval: browser_contentBlockingAllowListPrincipal.js expects private jars

Each private window is a jar of its own, told apart by its userContextId
(permissions-private-jar), so a private page's allow-list principal
names that jar, and an exception added in one private window holds in that
window alone. The private checks expect the origin suffix of the page's own
jar, and the storage access task adds its private exception in the window
it checks. The rest of the file runs as upstream's.

